    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 256\n\nTO THE SENATE:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nSenate Bill Number 3945-A, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to establishing the green\n      building credit\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This bill would amend the Tax Law to  provide  a  new,  non-refundable\nGreen Building Credit for eligible residential property equal to 100% of\nthe eligible costs, up to a maximum value of $10,000.\n\n  Construction  that meets the qualifications for green building certif-\nication is an important enterprise and is consistent  with  the  State's\nefforts  to  promote  and develop a sustainable and efficient energy and\nenvironmental  policy.  Under  existing  law,  however,   municipalities\nalready  have  the  option of granting a real property tax exemption for\nactivities substantially similar to those outlined in  the  legislation.\nFor  example,  municipalities  can opt-in to offer a green building real\nproperty tax exemption for new or reconstructed buildings  costing  more\nthan $10,000 that meet green building certification standards.\n\n  Moreover,  providing financial incentives for the development of green\nbuildings will have a significant revenue impact on the  State  that  is\nmore  appropriately  discussed  in  the context of the State budget. For\nthese reasons, I am therefore constrained to veto this bill.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
